  "final_message": "Task 1 is done and recorded in the ledger. `task-done` accepted it on the first try:\n\n`Task 1: complete (commits 843be5b..8cc238c, mutants: 3/3, tests: /private/tmp/msr104-venv/bin/python -m pytest -q \u2192 3 passed in 0.00s)`\n\n**What the first mutant run found:** mutant 2 survived. That mutant gives every left-over cent to the first person instead of one each. The plan's tests never have more than one cent left over, and with only one cent both versions give the same answer. So the tests didn't cover \"several cents left over\", which the spec's rule at `specs/split.md:9` includes.\n\n**Fix:**\n- I added `test_several_cents_left_over_go_one_each_to_the_first_people`, which checks that `split(1002, 4) == [251, 251, 250, 250]`. It passes on the real code and fails with mutant 2 applied. I didn't change the plan's two tests.\n- I added a row for that case to `task-1-mutants.md` and pointed mutant 2 at the new test.\n- Committed as `8cc238c`.\n\n**Second run** (`.sdd/plan/task-1-mutants-2.log`): 3 caught, 0 survived, 0 invalid. With the task's code taken back out, the test file can't import `bills`, so all three tests fail there, as they should.\n\nAs instructed, I haven't started the final review.",
